Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Public Announcement of Real Estate Values

CHAPTER 1 GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on the Public Announcement of Real Estate Values and matters necessary for its enforcement.

CHAPTER 2 PUBLIC ANNOUNCEMENT OF LAND PRICES

Article 2 (Selection of Standard Land)
(1) When selecting standard land pursuant to Article 3 (1) of the Act on the Public Announcement of Real Estate Values (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall select a parcel of land that can represent the relevant tract of land from among the parcels in that tract.
(2) Detailed criteria necessary for the selection and management of standard land under Article 3 (1) of the Act shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport following deliberation by the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values under Article 24 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values").

Article 3 (Base Date for Public Announcement of Standard Land Prices)
The base date for public announcement of standard land prices under Article 3 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "officially announced standard land prices") shall be January 1: Provided, That where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems it unavoidable in consideration of personnel for surveying and appraising officially announced standard land prices, etc., the Minister may designate certain areas and separately determine the base date for public announcement for those areas.

Article 4 (Methods of Public Announcement of Standard Land Prices)
(1) When publicly announcing standard land prices pursuant to Article 3 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall announce the following matters in the Official Gazette and post the officially announced standard land prices on the Real Estate Publicly Announced Price System operated by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport (hereinafter referred to as the "Real Estate Publicly Announced Price System"):
1. An outline of the matters specified in the subparagraphs of Article 5 of the Act;
2. Methods of inspecting officially announced standard land prices;
3. The period, procedures, and methods for filing objections.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems it necessary, the Minister may individually notify each owner of standard land (where there are multiple owners, this means each owner; hereinafter the same shall apply) of the officially announced standard land price and the period, procedures, and methods for filing objections. <Amended on June 2, 2020>
(3) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport does not provide notification under paragraph (2), the Minister shall make known, through broadcasting, newspapers, etc., that the announcement and posting under paragraph (1) have been made so that owners of standard land can inspect the officially announced standard land prices and file objections where necessary.

Article 5 (Procedures for Hearing Opinions of Owners of Standard Land)
(1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to hear the opinions of owners of standard land pursuant to Article 3 (2) of the Act, the Minister shall post the following matters on the Real Estate Publicly Announced Price System for at least 20 days: <Amended on October 8, 2020>
1. The subject of public announcement and the period and methods for inspection;
2. The period and methods for submitting opinions;
3. The proposed publicly announced prices appraised pursuant to Article 3 (5) of the Act by appraisal corporations, etc. (meaning appraisal corporations, etc. under subparagraph 4 of Article 2 of the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers; hereinafter the same shall apply).
(2) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall individually notify owners of standard land of the posting under paragraph (1): Provided, That where the standard land is the site of a building under the Act on Ownership and Management of Condominium Buildings, the Minister may notify the management body or manager under Article 23 or 24 of that Act and have the matters under paragraph (1) posted for at least seven days at a place suitable for providing notice, such as a bulletin board inside the building. <Amended on June 2, 2020>
(3) An owner of standard land who objects to a price posted pursuant to paragraph (1) may submit an opinion during the period for submitting opinions.

Article 6 (Criteria for Surveying and Appraising Officially Announced Standard Land Prices)
(1) The criteria for matters to be considered when the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport surveys and appraises officially announced standard land prices pursuant to Article 3 (4) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. In the case of transaction prices or rents of similar land in the vicinity: Where the relevant transaction or lease was concluded due to special circumstances of the parties or a lack of knowledge about land transactions or leases, the transaction price or rent that would have applied in the absence of such circumstances shall be used;
2. In the case of estimated costs necessary to develop land recognized as having a utility value similar to that of the relevant land: The standard development costs and ordinary incidental costs necessary to develop the relevant land as of the base date for public announcement shall be used.
(2) Where a building or other fixture exists on standard land, or a superficies or other right restricting the use of or profit from the land has been established, the officially announced standard land price shall be appraised on the assumption that the fixture or right does not exist.
(3) Detailed criteria necessary for surveying and appraising officially announced standard land prices, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 7 (Commissioning Surveys and Appraisals of Officially Announced Standard Land Prices)
(1) Pursuant to Article 3 (5) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall select persons to be commissioned to survey and appraise officially announced standard land prices from among appraisal corporations, etc. that meet all of the following requirements: <Amended on June 2, 2020; October 8, 2020>
1. Their business performance during the immediately preceding year, as of the date 30 days before the date of commissioning the survey and appraisal of officially announced standard land prices (hereinafter referred to as the "selection base date"), shall be at a level appropriate for performing surveys and appraisals of fair prices of standard land;
2. Their accounting audit procedures or system for reviewing appraisal reports shall be appropriate;
3. Business suspension dispositions, administrative fines, or disciplinary dispositions against affiliated certified appraisers under the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers shall not fall under any of the following criteria:
(a) Where the appraisal corporation, etc. has received at least three business suspension dispositions during the two years immediately preceding the selection base date;
(b) Where the appraisal corporation, etc. has received at least three administrative fine dispositions during the year immediately preceding the selection base date;
(c) Where the ratio of affiliated certified appraisers who received disciplinary dispositions during the year immediately preceding the selection base date is at least 10 percent of all affiliated certified appraisers as of the selection base date;
(d) Where, as of the selection base date, one year has not elapsed since the expiration of a period of business suspension.
(2) Detailed criteria concerning the requirements in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
(3) When allocating the volume of surveys and appraisals to each appraisal corporation, etc. selected pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall make the allocation proportionately based on the ratio of certified appraisers affiliated with the individual appraisal corporation, etc. (meaning those who can participate in the surveys and appraisals) to all certified appraisers affiliated with the selected appraisal corporations, etc. (meaning those who can participate in the surveys and appraisals): Provided, That the allocated volume may be adjusted according to the credibility of the appraisal corporation, etc., its diligence in previous surveys and appraisals of officially announced standard land prices, and whether its affiliated certified appraisers have received disciplinary dispositions. <Amended on October 8, 2020>
(4) "Standard land meeting the criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as cases where changes in land prices are small" in the proviso of Article 3 (5) of the Act means standard land in areas meeting all of the following requirements:
1. Areas where the rate of change in land prices by Eup/Myeon/Dong during the most recent year is not higher than the nationwide average rate of change in land prices;
2. Areas where there are no circumstances such as the implementation of a development project or a change in a land-use zone under subparagraph 15 of Article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act (hereinafter referred to as a "land-use zone") or a land-use district under subparagraph 16 of that Article (hereinafter referred to as a "land-use district").
(5) Detailed criteria necessary for the selection of appraisal corporations, etc. and the allocation of the volume of surveys and appraisals of fair prices of standard land, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (4), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on October 8, 2020>

Article 8 (Procedures for Surveying and Appraising Officially Announced Standard Land Prices)
(1) An appraisal corporation, etc. commissioned to survey and appraise officially announced standard land prices pursuant to Article 3 (5) of the Act shall survey and appraise such prices and other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, prepare a survey and appraisal report as prescribed by that Ordinance, and submit it to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on October 8, 2020>
(2) When preparing a survey and appraisal report pursuant to paragraph (1), an appraisal corporation, etc. shall hear in advance the opinions of the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governor, or Special Self-Governing Province Governor having jurisdiction over the relevant standard land (hereinafter referred to as a "Mayor/Do Governor"), and the head of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu (the head of a Gu refers to the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply). <Amended on October 8, 2020>
(3) A Mayor/Do Governor and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu requested to provide an opinion pursuant to paragraph (2) shall provide the opinion within 20 days from the date of the request. In such cases, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall provide the opinion following deliberation by the Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values under Article 25 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values"). <Amended on October 8, 2020>
(4) An officially announced standard land price shall be based on the arithmetic mean of the surveyed and appraised amounts in the reports submitted pursuant to paragraph (1).
(5) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may review the appropriateness of a report submitted pursuant to paragraph (1) using actual purchase and sale prices reported under Article 3 of the Act on Report on Real Estate Transactions, Etc. (hereinafter referred to as "reported actual transaction prices"), the appraisal information system under Article 9 of the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers (hereinafter referred to as the "appraisal information system"), etc. <Amended on January 17, 2017>
(6) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport determines that a report is inappropriate as a result of the review under paragraph (5), or where the highest of the surveyed and appraised amounts exceeds 1.3 times the lowest amount, the Minister may require the relevant appraisal corporation, etc. to correct and resubmit the report. <Amended on October 8, 2020>
(7) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport finds that the survey and appraisal in a report submitted pursuant to paragraph (1) were performed in violation of relevant statutes or regulations, the Minister shall notify the relevant appraisal corporation, etc. of the reasons and commission two other appraisal corporations, etc. to survey and appraise the relevant officially announced standard land price again. In such cases, the fair price of the standard land shall be based on the arithmetic mean of the amounts obtained through the new surveys and appraisals. <Amended on June 2, 2020; October 8, 2020>

Article 9 (Cooperation in Surveys of Fair Prices of Standard Land)
"Relevant materials prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as registered matters under individual statutes" in the former part of Article 4 of the Act means the following materials (excluding resident registration numbers under Article 7-2 (1) of the Resident Registration Act and alien registration numbers under Article 31 (5) of the Immigration Act contained in those materials): <Amended on October 8, 2020>
1. Building registers under the Building Act (including drawings showing current conditions);
2. Cadastral maps, forest land maps, orthophoto maps, land registers, and forest land registers under the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data;
3. Certificates of land-use plans under the Framework Act on the Regulation of Land Use (including accompanying confirmation maps);
4. Topographic maps of urban or Gun management plans under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act (including electronic maps);
5. Registers under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Registration of Real Estate Act;
6. Actual transaction prices reported under Article 3 of the Act on Report on Real Estate Transactions, Etc.;
7. Information and materials registered in the appraisal information system pursuant to the main clause of Article 9 (2) of the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers;
8. Materials concerning lease agreements in the register of fixed dates under the former part of Article 4 (2) of the Commercial Building Lease Protection Act;
9. The status of authorization and permission for development projects by administrative district;
10. The names and addresses of owners of standard land;
11. Other materials prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as necessary for selecting standard land or surveying and appraising fair prices of standard land.

Article 10 (Matters to Be Publicly Announced Concerning Standard Land Prices)
(1) The unit area under subparagraph 2 of Article 5 of the Act shall be one square meter.
(2) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 5 of Article 5 of the Act means the following matters concerning standard land:
1. Land category;
2. Land-use zone;
3. Road conditions;
4. Other matters necessary for the public announcement of standard land prices.

Article 11 (Preparation and Supply of Books, etc. Concerning Officially Announced Standard Land Prices)
(1) Books, charts, etc. supplied by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to relevant administrative agencies, etc. pursuant to Article 6 of the Act shall include the matters specified in the subparagraphs of Article 5 of the Act.
(2) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may prepare and supply the books, charts, etc. under paragraph (1) as records on special media, such as electronic records.

Article 12 (Objections to Officially Announced Standard Land Prices)
A person who intends to file an objection to an officially announced standard land price pursuant to Article 7 (1) of the Act shall submit an objection application to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by documents proving the grounds for the objection.

Article 13 (Application of Officially Announced Standard Land Prices)
(1) "Public organizations prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 1 (c) of Article 8 of the Act means the following institutions or organizations: <Amended on April 2, 2019>
1. Forestry cooperatives and the National Forestry Cooperative Federation under the Forestry Cooperatives Act;
2. Cooperatives and the National Agricultural Cooperative Federation under the Agricultural Cooperatives Act;
3. Fisheries cooperatives and the National Federation of Fisheries Cooperatives under the Fisheries Cooperatives Act;
4. The Korea Rural Community Corporation under the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act;
5. The Korea SMEs and Startups Agency under the Small and Medium Enterprises Promotion Act;
6. Industrial complex management corporations under the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act.
(2) "Calculation of land prices prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 2 (c) of Article 8 of the Act means the calculation of land prices for the following purposes:
1. Supply or allotment of land, etc. developed pursuant to the National Land Planning and Utilization Act or other statutes or regulations;
2. Sale of replotted land or land reserved to cover project costs, or applications for replotting, for any of the following projects:
(a) Urban development projects under Article 2 (1) 2 of the Urban Development Act;
(b) Improvement projects under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments;
(c) Agricultural production infrastructure improvement projects under subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Agricultural and Fishing Villages Improvement Act.
3. Management, purchase, sale, auction, or revaluation of land.

Article 14 (Unit Area for Officially Announced Individual Land Prices)
The unit area under Article 10 (1) of the Act shall be one square meter.

Article 15 (Land for Which Individual Land Prices Need Not Be Publicly Announced)
(1) Pursuant to the former part of Article 10 (2) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu may refrain from determining and publicly announcing individual land prices under Article 10 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "officially announced individual land prices") for land falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Land selected as standard land;
2. Land not subject to farmland preservation charges, development charges, or similar charges;
3. Land not subject to national or local taxes (in the case of State-owned or publicly owned land, limited to land for public use).
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall determine and publicly announce individual land prices for land falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Land for which relevant statutes or regulations require officially announced individual land prices to be applied to the calculation of land prices, etc.;
2. Land for which the head of the Si/Gun/Gu has decided, in consultation with the head of the relevant administrative agency, to determine and publicly announce an individual land price.

Article 16 (Land for Which a Different Base Date for Public Announcement of Individual Land Prices May Be Set)
(1) Land for which a different base date for public announcement of individual land prices may be set pursuant to Article 10 (3) of the Act shall be land falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Land subdivided or merged pursuant to the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data;
2. Land newly registered pursuant to the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data as a result of reclamation of public waters, etc.;
3. Land whose land category has been changed pursuant to the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data due to an alteration of the form and quality of the land or a change of use;
4. Land converted from State or public ownership to private ownership through sale, etc. for which no officially announced individual land price exists.
(2) "Date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10 (3) of the Act means the date specified in the following subparagraphs:
1. Land for which a ground specified in any subparagraph of paragraph (1) arises between January 1 and June 30: July 1 of that year;
2. Land for which a ground specified in any subparagraph of paragraph (1) arises between July 1 and December 31: January 1 of the following year.

Article 17 (Criteria for Surveying and Calculating Officially Announced Individual Land Prices)
(1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall establish criteria for surveying and calculating officially announced individual land prices under Article 10 (4) of the Act and notify the heads of Sis/Guns/Gus thereof, and the heads of Sis/Guns/Gus shall survey and calculate officially announced individual land prices in accordance with those criteria.
(2) The criteria under paragraph (1) shall include the following matters: <Amended on October 8, 2020>
1. Matters concerning surveys of land characteristics affecting the formation of land prices;
2. Matters concerning the selection of standard land serving as the basis for calculating officially announced individual land prices (hereinafter referred to as "comparative standard land");
3. Matters concerning use of the land price comparison table under Article 3 (8) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "land price comparison table");
4. Other matters necessary for surveying and calculating officially announced individual land prices.

Article 18 (Verification of Officially Announced Individual Land Prices)
(1) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu commissions verification of the appropriateness of individual land prices pursuant to the main clause of Article 10 (5) of the Act, he or she shall provide maps showing the land prices and land price survey materials for all individual land prices calculated pursuant to paragraph (4) of that Article.
(2) Appraisal corporations, etc. commissioned to perform verification pursuant to the main clause of Article 10 (5) of the Act shall review and confirm the following matters and present their opinions: <Amended on October 8, 2020>
1. Matters concerning the appropriateness of the selection of comparative standard land;
2. Matters concerning the appropriateness of the calculation of individual land prices;
3. Matters concerning the maintenance of balance between the calculated individual land prices and officially announced standard land prices;
4. Matters concerning the maintenance of balance between the calculated individual land prices and the prices of neighboring land;
5. Whether the land characteristics are consistent with those considered when calculating standard housing prices, individual housing prices, standard non-residential real estate prices, and individual non-residential real estate prices;
6. Whether major characteristics applied when calculating individual land prices, such as land-use zones and the actual use of the land, are consistent with official records;
7. Other matters that the head of the Si/Gun/Gu has requested to be reviewed.
(3) When omitting verification by appraisal corporations, etc. pursuant to the proviso of Article 10 (5) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall select the relevant parcels in ascending order of the difference between the rate of change in the price of the individual parcel and the annual average rate of change in land prices in the Eup/Myeon/Dong where the land is located (meaning the annual average rate of change in land prices surveyed and published by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport): Provided, That land for which circumstances exist such as the implementation of a development project or a change in a land-use zone or land-use district shall not be selected for omission of verification. <Amended on October 8, 2020>
(4) Detailed matters necessary for verification of individual land prices, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (3), shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. In such cases, the Minister shall consult in advance with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies regarding omission of verification.

Article 19 (Hearing Opinions of Owners of Individual Parcels, etc.)
(1) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to hear the opinions of landowners and other interested persons (hereinafter referred to as "owners of individual parcels, etc.") concerning the calculation of individual land prices pursuant to Article 10 (5) of the Act, he or she shall make an individual land price inspection register available and post the following matters on the bulletin board or website of the relevant Si, Gun, or Gu (a Gu means an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply) for at least 20 days so that owners of individual parcels, etc. can inspect the individual land prices:
1. The period and place for inspection;
2. The period and methods for submitting opinions.
(2) An owner of an individual parcel, etc. who has an opinion concerning an individual land price inspected pursuant to paragraph (1) may submit the opinion to the head of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu during the period for submitting opinions.
(3) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu receives an opinion pursuant to paragraph (2), he or she shall examine it within 30 days from the expiration of the period for submitting opinions and notify the person who submitted the opinion of the result.
(4) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu may conduct an on-site survey and verification when conducting an examination under paragraph (3).

Article 20 (Appraisal Corporations, etc. Performing Verification)
"Appraisal corporations, etc. with excellent appraisal performance, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10 (6) of the Act means appraisal corporations, etc. that meet all the requirements specified in the subparagraphs of Article 7 (1). <Amended on October 8, 2020>

Article 21 (Determination and Public Announcement of Individual Land Prices)
(1) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall determine and publicly announce individual land prices by May 31 each year: Provided, That in cases under Article 16 (2) 1, such prices shall be determined and publicly announced by October 31 of that year, and in cases under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph, by May 31 of the following year.
(2) When publicly announcing individual land prices pursuant to paragraph (1), the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall post the following matters on the bulletin board or website of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu:
1. Matters concerning the determination of officially announced individual land prices, such as the survey base date, the number of parcels covered by the announcement, and methods of inspecting the officially announced individual land prices;
2. The period, procedures, and methods for filing objections.
(3) Article 4 (2) and (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to notification of officially announced individual land prices, objection periods, etc.

Article 22 (Objections to Officially Announced Individual Land Prices)
(1) A person who intends to file an objection to an officially announced individual land price pursuant to Article 11 (1) of the Act shall submit an objection application to the head of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu, accompanied by documents proving the grounds for the objection.
(2) Where necessary to examine an objection submitted pursuant to paragraph (1), the head of a Si/Gun/Gu may commission an appraisal corporation, etc. to perform verification. <Amended on October 8, 2020>

Article 23 (Grounds for Correction of Officially Announced Individual Land Prices)
(1) "Obvious errors prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where the public announcement procedures under Article 10 of the Act have not been fully followed;
2. Where major factors affecting land prices, such as land-use zones or land-use districts, have been incorrectly surveyed;
3. Where there is an error in the application of the land price comparison table.
(2) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to correct an error in an officially announced individual land price pursuant to Article 12 of the Act, he or she shall determine and publicly announce the corrections following deliberation by the Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values: Provided, That in cases of miscalculation or clerical error, deliberation by the Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values may be omitted.

Article 24 (Subsidies for Costs of Determining and Publicly Announcing Individual Land Prices)
Costs that may be subsidized by the National Treasury pursuant to Article 14 of the Act shall not exceed 50 percent of the costs of determining and publicly announcing individual land prices.

Article 25 (Surveys of Real Estate Price Information, etc.)
The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may conduct surveys of the following matters at appropriate intervals pursuant to Article 15 (1) of the Act:
1. Surveys of trends in prices, such as purchase and sale prices and rents, of land and housing;
2. Surveys of lease-related information concerning non-residential real estate, such as rents, management expenses, and premiums, and rental market trends, such as vacancy rates and investment returns.

CHAPTER 3 PUBLIC ANNOUNCEMENT OF HOUSING PRICES

Article 26 (Selection of Standard Houses)
(1) When selecting standard houses pursuant to Article 16(1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall select houses that can represent the relevant group of detached houses from among a group of detached houses generally recognized as similar.
(2) Detailed criteria necessary for the selection and management of standard houses under Article 16(1) of the Act shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport after deliberation by the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values.

Article 27 (Base Date for Public Announcement of Standard Housing Prices) The base date for public announcement of standard housing prices under Article 16(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "standard housing prices") shall be January 1. Provided, That where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems it unavoidable in consideration of the personnel available to survey and calculate standard housing prices, the number of standard houses, etc., the Minister may designate certain areas and separately determine the base date for public announcement for those areas.

Article 28 (Methods of Public Announcement of Standard Housing Prices)
(1) When publicly announcing standard housing prices pursuant to Article 16(1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall publish the following matters in the Official Gazette and post the standard housing prices on the Real Estate Publicly Announced Price System:
1. An outline of the matters specified in each subparagraph of Article 16(2) of the Act;
2. Methods of inspecting standard housing prices;
3. The period, procedures, and methods for filing objections.
(2) Article 4(2) and (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to notification of standard housing prices, the period for filing objections, etc.

Article 29 (Matters to Be Publicly Announced Regarding Standard Housing Prices) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 16(2)5 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Land category;
2. Land-use zone;
3. Road conditions;
4. Other matters necessary for the public announcement of standard housing prices.

Article 30 (Procedures for Surveying and Calculating Standard Housing Prices)
(1) The Korea Real Estate Board under the Korea Real Estate Board Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Board"), upon being commissioned to survey and calculate standard housing prices pursuant to Article 16(4) of the Act, shall survey and calculate standard housing prices and other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, and then prepare a report on the survey and calculation of standard housing prices as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport and submit it to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on December 8, 2020>
(2) When preparing a survey and calculation report pursuant to paragraph (1), the Board shall hear in advance the opinions of the Mayor/Do Governor and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the location of the relevant standard house. <Amended on October 8, 2020; December 8, 2020>
(3) Upon being requested to present opinions pursuant to paragraph (2), the Mayor/Do Governor and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall present their opinions within 20 days from the date of the request. In such cases, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall present opinions after deliberation by the Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values. <Amended on October 8, 2020>
(4) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may review the appropriateness of reports submitted pursuant to paragraph (1) by using reported actual transaction prices, appraisal information system, etc.
(5) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport determines, as a result of the review under paragraph (4), that a report is inappropriate or finds that the survey and calculation of standard housing prices was conducted in violation of relevant statutes or regulations, the Minister may require the Board to correct and resubmit the report. <Amended on December 8, 2020>

Article 31 (Criteria for Surveying and Calculating Standard Housing Prices)
(1) The criteria for matters to be taken into consideration when the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport surveys and calculates standard housing prices pursuant to Article 16(5) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. In the case of transaction prices or rents of similar detached houses in the vicinity: Where a transaction or lease was concluded due to special circumstances of the parties or a lack of knowledge concerning transactions or leases of detached houses, the transaction price or rent that would have been agreed upon in the absence of such circumstances shall be used as the basis;
2. In the case of estimated costs necessary to construct a detached house recognized as having a use value similar to that of the relevant detached house: The standard construction costs and ordinary incidental expenses required to construct the relevant detached house as of the base date for public announcement shall be used.
(2) Where a right of lease on a deposit basis or any other right restricting the use of or the receipt of profits from a detached house has been established on a standard house, its fair price shall be calculated on the assumption that such right does not exist.
(3) Detailed criteria necessary for surveying and calculating standard housing prices, other than the matters prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 32 (Detached Houses for Which Individual Housing Prices Need Not Be Publicly Announced)
(1) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu may refrain from determining and publicly announcing individual housing prices (meaning individual housing prices under Article 17(1) of the Act; hereinafter the same shall apply) for detached houses falling under any of the following subparagraphs pursuant to the former part of Article 17(2) of the Act:
1. Detached houses selected as standard houses;
2. Detached houses not subject to national or local taxes.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall determine and publicly announce individual housing prices for detached houses falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Detached houses for which relevant statutes or regulations require individual housing prices to be applied when calculating the prices of detached houses, etc.;
2. Detached houses for which the head of a Si/Gun/Gu has decided, in consultation with the heads of relevant administrative agencies, to determine and publicly announce individual housing prices.

Article 33 (Matters to Be Publicly Announced Regarding Individual Housing Prices) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 17(3)3 of the Act means the following matters:
1. The use and area of the individual house;
2. Other matters necessary for the public announcement of individual housing prices.

Article 34 (Detached Houses for Which a Different Base Date for Public Announcement of Individual Housing Prices May Be Set)
(1) Detached houses for which a different base date for public announcement of individual housing prices may be set pursuant to Article 17(4) of the Act shall be detached houses falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Detached houses whose sites have been subdivided or merged pursuant to the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data;
2. Detached houses that have undergone construction, major repairs, or a change of use under the Building Act;
3. Detached houses that have become privately owned through the sale, etc. of State-owned or publicly owned detached houses and for which there are no individual housing prices.
(2) "Date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 17(4) of the Act means the date specified in the following subparagraphs:
1. Detached houses for which any of the grounds specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) arose between January 1 and May 31: June 1 of the same year;
2. Detached houses for which any of the grounds specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) arose between June 1 and December 31: January 1 of the following year.

Article 35 (Procedures for Surveying and Calculating Individual Housing Prices)
(1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall establish the criteria for surveying and calculating individual housing prices under Article 17(5) of the Act and notify the head of a Si/Gun/Gu thereof, and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall survey and calculate individual housing prices in accordance with those criteria.
(2) The criteria under paragraph (1) shall include the following matters:
1. Matters concerning surveys of housing characteristics that affect housing price formation;
2. Matters concerning the selection of standard houses that serve as the basis for calculating individual housing prices (hereinafter referred to as "comparative standard houses");
3. Matters concerning the use of the housing price comparison table under Article 16(6) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "housing price comparison table");
4. Other matters necessary for surveying and calculating individual housing prices.

Article 36 (Verification of Individual Housing Prices)
(1) When commissioning the Board to verify the validity of individual housing prices pursuant to the main clause of Article 17(6) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall provide price status maps and price survey data for all individual housing prices calculated pursuant to paragraph (1) of that Article. <Amended on December 8, 2020>
(2) The Board commissioned to conduct verification pursuant to the main clause of Article 17(6) of the Act shall review and confirm the following matters and present its opinions thereon: <Amended on October 8, 2020; December 8, 2020>
1. Matters concerning the appropriateness of the selection of comparative standard houses;
2. Matters concerning the appropriateness of the calculation of individual housing prices;
3. Matters concerning the maintenance of a balance between the calculated individual housing prices and standard housing prices;
4. Matters concerning the maintenance of a balance between the calculated individual housing prices and the individual housing prices of neighboring houses;
5. Whether the land characteristics are consistent with those taken into consideration when calculating officially announced standard land prices and officially announced individual land prices;
6. Whether major characteristics applied when calculating individual housing prices, such as land-use zones and land use conditions, are consistent with public records;
7. Other matters for which the head of a Si/Gun/Gu has requested a review.
(3) When omitting verification by the Board pursuant to the proviso to Article 17(6) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall select the houses concerned in ascending order of the difference between the rate of change in individual housing prices and the average annual rate of change in housing prices in the Si, Gun, or Gu where the relevant detached house is located (meaning the average annual rate of change in housing prices surveyed and published by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport). Provided, That houses affected by such circumstances as the implementation of a development project or a change in land-use zones or land-use districts shall not be selected as houses for which verification is to be omitted. <Amended on December 8, 2020>
(4) Detailed matters necessary for the verification of individual housing prices, other than the matters prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (3), shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. In such cases, the Minister shall consult in advance with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies regarding the omission of verification.

Article 37 (Hearing Opinions of Owners of Individual Houses, etc.) Article 19 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the hearing of opinions under the main clause of Article 17(6) of the Act.

Article 38 (Determination and Public Announcement of Individual Housing Prices)
(1) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall determine and publicly announce individual housing prices by April 30 each year. Provided, That in cases falling under Article 34(2)1, such prices shall be determined and publicly announced by September 30 of the same year, and in cases falling under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph, by April 30 of the following year.
(2) When publicly announcing individual housing prices pursuant to paragraph (1), the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall post the following matters on the bulletin board or website of the relevant Si, Gun, or Gu:
1. Matters concerning the determination of individual housing prices, such as the base date for the survey and methods of inspecting individual housing prices;
2. The period, procedures, and methods for filing objections.
(3) Article 4(2) and (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the methods of public announcement of and notification of individual housing prices.

Article 39 (Subsidies for Costs of Determining and Publicly Announcing Individual Housing Prices) Article 24 shall apply mutatis mutandis to subsidies for the costs of determining and publicly announcing individual housing prices.

Article 40 (Base Date for Public Announcement of Multi-Family Housing Prices) The base date for public announcement of multi-family housing prices under the main clause of Article 18(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "multi-family housing prices") shall be January 1. Provided, That where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems it unavoidable in consideration of the personnel available to survey and calculate multi-family housing prices, the number of multi-family housing units, etc., the Minister may designate certain areas and separately determine the base date for public announcement for those areas.

Article 41 (Cases Where the Commissioner of the National Tax Service Separately Gives Public Notice of Multi-Family Housing Prices) Cases where the Commissioner of the National Tax Service separately determines and gives public notice of multi-family housing prices pursuant to the proviso to Article 18(1) of the Act shall be cases where, after consulting with the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport on the timing, properties concerned, etc., the Commissioner determines and gives public notice of the standard market values of multi-family housing falling under any of the following subparagraphs pursuant to the proviso to Article 99(1)1(d) of the Income Tax Act and the proviso to the portion of Article 61(1)4 other than its subitems of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act:
1. Apartment buildings;
2. Row houses with a total floor area of at least 165 square meters.

Article 42 (Hearing Opinions of Owners of Multi-Family Housing, etc.) Article 5(1) and (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the hearing of opinions under Article 18(2) of the Act.

Article 43 (Calculation and Public Announcement of Multi-Family Housing Prices)
(1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall calculate and publicly announce multi-family housing prices by April 30 each year. Provided, That in cases falling under Article 44(2)1, such prices shall be publicly announced by September 30 of the same year, and in cases falling under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph, by April 30 of the following year.
(2) The public announcement of multi-family housing prices under Article 18(1) of the Act shall include the following matters:
1. The location, name, building number, and unit number of the multi-family housing;
2. The multi-family housing price;
3. The area of the multi-family housing;
4. Other matters necessary for the public announcement of multi-family housing prices.
(3) When publicly announcing multi-family housing prices pursuant to the main clause of Article 18(1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall publish the following matters in the Official Gazette and post the multi-family housing prices on the Real Estate Publicly Announced Price System. In such cases, Article 4(2) and (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to notification of multi-family housing prices:
1. An outline of the matters specified in each subparagraph of paragraph (2);
2. Methods of inspecting multi-family housing prices;
3. The period, procedures, and methods for filing objections.
(4) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall provide the matters publicly announced concerning multi-family housing prices pursuant to the main clause of Article 18(1) of the Act to the following persons within 10 days from the date of the notice under paragraph (3): <Amended on July 26, 2017>
1. The Minister of the Interior and Safety;
2. The Commissioner of the National Tax Service;
3. The head of a Si/Gun/Gu.

Article 44 (Multi-Family Housing for Which a Different Base Date for Public Announcement of Multi-Family Housing Prices May Be Set)
(1) Multi-family housing for which a different base date for public announcement of multi-family housing prices may be set pursuant to Article 18(4) of the Act shall be multi-family housing falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Multi-family housing whose sites have been subdivided or merged pursuant to the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data;
2. Multi-family housing that has undergone construction, major repairs, or a change of use under the Building Act;
3. Multi-family housing that has become privately owned through the sale, etc. of State-owned or publicly owned multi-family housing and for which there are no multi-family housing prices.
(2) "Date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 18(4) of the Act means the date specified in the following subparagraphs:
1. Multi-family housing for which any of the grounds specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) arose between January 1 and May 31: June 1 of the same year;
2. Multi-family housing for which any of the grounds specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) arose between June 1 and December 31: January 1 of the following year.

Article 45 (Criteria for Surveying and Calculating Multi-Family Housing Prices)
(1) The criteria for matters to be taken into consideration when the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport surveys and calculates multi-family housing prices pursuant to Article 18(5) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. In the case of transaction prices or rents of similar multi-family housing in the vicinity: Where a transaction or lease was concluded due to special circumstances of the parties or a lack of knowledge concerning transactions or leases of multi-family housing, the transaction price or rent that would have been agreed upon in the absence of such circumstances shall be used as the basis;
2. In the case of estimated costs necessary to construct multi-family housing recognized as having a use value similar to that of the relevant multi-family housing: The standard construction costs and ordinary incidental expenses required to construct the relevant multi-family housing as of the base date for public announcement shall be used.
(2) Where a right of lease on a deposit basis or any other right restricting the use of or the receipt of profits from multi-family housing has been established on multi-family housing, its fair price shall be calculated on the assumption that such right does not exist.
(3) Detailed criteria necessary for surveying and calculating multi-family housing prices, other than the matters prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 46 (Procedures for Surveying and Calculating Multi-Family Housing Prices)
(1) The Board, upon being commissioned to survey and calculate multi-family housing prices pursuant to Article 18(6) of the Act, shall survey and calculate multi-family housing prices and other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, and then prepare a report on the survey and calculation of multi-family housing prices as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport and submit it to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on December 8, 2020>
(2) When preparing a survey and calculation report pursuant to paragraph (1), the Board shall hear in advance the opinions of the Mayor/Do Governor and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the location of the relevant multi-family housing. <Newly Inserted on August 20, 2024>
(3) Upon being requested to present opinions pursuant to paragraph (2), the Mayor/Do Governor and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall present their opinions within 20 days from the date of the request. In such cases, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall present opinions after deliberation by the Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values. <Newly Inserted on August 20, 2024>
(4) Upon receiving a report submitted pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall provide the report to the following persons: <Amended on July 26, 2017; October 8, 2020; August 20, 2024>
1. The Minister of the Interior and Safety;
2. The Commissioner of the National Tax Service;
3. The Mayor/Do Governor;
4. The head of a Si/Gun/Gu.
(5) A person provided with a report pursuant to paragraph (4) may request the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to review the appropriateness of the report. <Amended on August 20, 2024>
(6) Article 30(4) and (5) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the review of the appropriateness of reports submitted pursuant to paragraph (1) and to the correction of such reports. <Amended on August 20, 2024>

Article 47 (Grounds for Correction of Multi-Family Housing Prices)
(1) "Obvious errors prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 18(7) of the Act means cases falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Where the procedures for public announcement under Article 18 of the Act have not been fully followed;
2. Where surveys of major factors affecting multi-family housing prices, such as the identification of building and unit numbers and floors, have been conducted incorrectly.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to correct an error in a multi-family housing price pursuant to Article 18(7) of the Act, the Minister shall determine and publicly announce the corrections after deliberation by the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values. Provided, That deliberation by the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values may be omitted in cases of calculation errors or clerical errors.

CHAPTER 4 PUBLIC ANNOUNCEMENT OF NON-RESIDENTIAL REAL ESTATE PRICES

Article 48 (Selection of Standard Non-Residential Real Estate)
(1) When selecting standard non-residential real estate pursuant to Article 20(1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall select real estate that can represent the relevant group of general non-residential real estate from among a group of general non-residential real estate. In such cases, the Minister shall hear in advance the opinions of the Mayor/Do Governor and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu in whose jurisdiction the relevant standard non-residential real estate is located.
(2) Detailed criteria necessary for the selection and management of standard non-residential real estate under Article 20(1) of the Act shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport after deliberation by the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values.

Article 49 (Base Date for Public Announcement of Standard Non-Residential Real Estate Prices) The base date for public announcement of standard non-residential real estate prices under Article 20(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "standard non-residential real estate prices") shall be January 1. Provided, That where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems it unavoidable in consideration of the personnel available to survey and calculate standard non-residential real estate prices, the number of standard non-residential real estate properties, etc., the Minister may designate certain areas and separately determine and give public notice of the base date for public announcement for those areas.

Article 50 (Methods of Public Announcement of Standard Non-Residential Real Estate Prices)
(1) When publicly announcing standard non-residential real estate prices pursuant to Article 20(1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall publish the following matters in the Official Gazette and post the standard non-residential real estate prices on the Real Estate Publicly Announced Price System:
1. An outline of the matters specified in each subparagraph of Article 20(2) of the Act;
2. Methods of inspecting standard non-residential real estate prices;
3. The period, procedures, and methods for filing objections.
(2) Article 4(2) and (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to notification of standard non-residential real estate prices, the period for filing objections, etc.

Article 51 (Matters to Be Publicly Announced Regarding Standard Non-Residential Real Estate Prices) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 20(2)5 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Land category;
2. Land-use zone;
3. Road conditions;
4. Other matters necessary for the public announcement of standard non-residential real estate prices.

Article 52 (Institution to Be Commissioned to Survey and Calculate Standard Non-Residential Real Estate Prices) "A person with expertise in surveying and calculating real estate prices, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 20(4) of the Act means the Board. <Amended on December 8, 2020>

Article 53 (Procedures for Surveying and Calculating Standard Non-Residential Real Estate Prices)
(1) A person commissioned to survey and calculate standard non-residential real estate prices pursuant to Article 20(4) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "institution for surveying and calculating standard non-residential real estate prices") shall survey and calculate standard non-residential real estate prices and other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, and then prepare a report on the survey and calculation of standard non-residential real estate prices as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport and submit it to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
(2) When preparing a survey and calculation report pursuant to paragraph (1), an institution for surveying and calculating standard non-residential real estate prices shall hear in advance the opinions of the Mayor/Do Governor and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the location of the relevant real estate.
(3) Upon being requested to present opinions pursuant to paragraph (2), the Mayor/Do Governor and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall present their opinions within 20 days from the date of the request. In such cases, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall present opinions after deliberation by the Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values.
(4) Article 30(4) and (5) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the review of the appropriateness of reports on the survey and calculation of standard non-residential real estate prices under paragraph (1) and to the correction of such reports.

Article 54 (Criteria for Surveying and Calculating Standard Non-Residential Real Estate Prices)
(1) The criteria for matters to be taken into consideration when the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport surveys and calculates standard non-residential real estate prices pursuant to Article 20(5) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. In the case of transaction prices or rents of similar general non-residential real estate in the vicinity: Where a transaction or lease was concluded due to special circumstances of the parties or a lack of knowledge concerning transactions or leases of general non-residential real estate, the transaction price or rent that would have been agreed upon in the absence of such circumstances shall be used as the basis;
2. In the case of estimated costs necessary to construct general non-residential real estate recognized as having a use value similar to that of the relevant general non-residential real estate: The standard construction costs and ordinary incidental expenses required to construct the relevant general non-residential real estate as of the base date for public announcement shall be used.
(2) Where a right of lease on a deposit basis or any other right restricting the use of or the receipt of profits from general non-residential real estate has been established on general non-residential real estate, its fair price shall be surveyed and calculated on the assumption that such right does not exist.
(3) Detailed criteria necessary for surveying and calculating standard non-residential real estate prices, other than the matters prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 55 (Cases Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Commissioner of the National Tax Service Determines and Gives Public Notice of Individual Non-Residential Real Estate Prices) Cases where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Commissioner of the National Tax Service separately determines and gives public notice of individual non-residential real estate prices under the main clause of Article 21(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "individual non-residential real estate prices") pursuant to the proviso to that paragraph shall be cases where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Commissioner of the National Tax Service separately determines and gives public notice of individual non-residential real estate prices after consulting in advance with the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport on the properties concerned, timing, etc. <Amended on July 26, 2017>

Article 56 (General Non-residential Real Estate for Which Individual Non-residential Real Estate Prices Need Not Be Publicly Announced)
(1) Pursuant to the former part of Article 21 (2) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu may choose not to determine and publicly announce individual non-residential real estate prices for general non-residential real estate falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. General non-residential real estate selected as standard non-residential real estate;
2. General non-residential real estate that is not subject to national or local taxes;
3. Other general non-residential real estate prescribed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall publicly announce individual non-residential real estate prices for general non-residential real estate falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. General non-residential real estate for which relevant statutes and regulations require the application of individual non-residential real estate prices to the calculation of prices of general non-residential real estate, etc.;
2. General non-residential real estate for which the head of a Si/Gun/Gu has decided, in consultation with the heads of relevant administrative agencies, to determine and publicly announce individual non-residential real estate prices.

Article 57 (Matters to Be Publicly Announced concerning Individual Non-residential Real Estate Prices)
The term "matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21 (3) 3 of the Act means the following matters:
1. The use and area of individual non-residential real estate;
2. Other matters necessary for the public announcement of individual non-residential real estate prices.

Article 58 (General Non-residential Real Estate for Which a Different Base Date for Public Announcement of Individual Non-residential Real Estate Prices May Be Set)
(1) General non-residential real estate for which a different base date for public announcement of individual non-residential real estate prices may be set pursuant to Article 21 (4) of the Act shall be real estate falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. General non-residential real estate whose site has been divided or consolidated pursuant to the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data;
2. General non-residential real estate that has undergone construction, substantial repair, or a change of use under the Building Act;
3. General non-residential real estate that has become privately owned through sale or otherwise after being owned by the State or a local government and for which there is no individual non-residential real estate price.
(2) The term "date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21 (4) of the Act means the date specified in the following subparagraphs:
1. General non-residential real estate for which a ground specified in any subparagraph of paragraph (1) arose between January 1 and May 31: June 1 of that year;
2. General non-residential real estate for which a ground specified in any subparagraph of paragraph (1) arose between June 1 and December 31: January 1 of the following year.

Article 59 (Procedures for Surveying and Calculating Individual Non-residential Real Estate Prices)
(1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall establish standards for surveying and calculating individual non-residential real estate prices under Article 21 (5) of the Act and notify the heads of Sis/Guns/Gus thereof, and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall survey and calculate individual non-residential real estate prices in accordance with those standards.
(2) The standards under paragraph (1) shall include the following matters:
1. Matters concerning surveys of the characteristics of general non-residential real estate that affect the formation of general non-residential real estate prices;
2. Matters concerning the selection of standard non-residential real estate that serves as the basis for calculating individual non-residential real estate prices (hereinafter referred to as "comparative standard non-residential real estate");
3. Matters concerning the use of the non-residential real estate price comparison table under Article 20 (6) of the Act;
4. Other matters necessary for surveying and calculating individual non-residential real estate prices.

Article 60 (Verification of Individual Non-residential Real Estate Prices)
(1) When requesting verification of individual non-residential real estate prices pursuant to the main clause of Article 21 (6) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall provide maps showing the price status and price survey data for all individual non-residential real estate prices calculated pursuant to paragraph (1) of that Article.
(2) The term "persons prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as persons requested to survey and calculate standard non-residential real estate prices under Article 20" in the main clause of Article 21 (6) of the Act means any of the following persons: <Amended on October 8, 2020; December 8, 2020>
1. Appraisal corporations, etc.;
2. The Board.
(3) A person requested to conduct verification pursuant to the main clause of Article 21 (6) of the Act shall review and confirm the following matters and present an opinion: <Amended on October 8, 2020>
1. Matters concerning the appropriateness of the selection of comparative standard non-residential real estate;
2. Matters concerning the appropriateness of the calculation of individual non-residential real estate prices;
3. Matters concerning maintaining balance between the calculated individual non-residential real estate prices and standard non-residential real estate prices;
4. Matters concerning maintaining balance between the calculated individual non-residential real estate prices and the individual non-residential real estate prices of nearby general non-residential real estate;
5. Whether the land characteristics are consistent with those taken into account in calculating officially announced standard land prices and officially announced individual land prices;
6. Whether major characteristics applied in calculating individual non-residential real estate prices, such as land-use zones and the status of land use, are consistent with official records;
7. Other matters for which the head of a Si/Gun/Gu has requested a review.
(4) When omitting verification pursuant to the proviso to Article 21 (6) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall select the general non-residential real estate concerned in ascending order of the difference between the rate of change in its individual non-residential real estate price and the average annual rate of change in individual non-residential real estate prices in the Si/Gun/Gu where the relevant general non-residential real estate is located (meaning the average annual rate of change in individual non-residential real estate prices surveyed and published by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport). Provided, That general non-residential real estate for which there are grounds such as the implementation of a development project or a change in a land-use zone or land-use district shall not be selected as real estate for which verification is to be omitted.
(5) Detailed matters necessary for the verification of individual non-residential real estate prices, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (4), shall be prescribed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. In such cases, the Minister shall consult in advance with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies regarding the omission of verification.

Article 61 (Hearing Opinions of Owners, etc. of General Non-residential Real Estate)
Article 19 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the hearing of opinions under the main clause of Article 21 (6) of the Act.

Article 62 (Determination and Public Announcement of Individual Non-residential Real Estate Prices)
(1) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to determine and publicly announce individual non-residential real estate prices, the head shall determine and publicly announce such prices by April 30 of each year. Provided, That the prices shall be determined and publicly announced by September 30 of that year in the case of Article 58 (2) 1 and by April 30 of the following year in the case of subparagraph 2 of that paragraph.
(2) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu who publicly announces individual non-residential real estate prices pursuant to paragraph (1) shall individually notify the owners of individual non-residential real estate of the following matters:
1. Matters concerning the determination of individual non-residential real estate prices, such as the survey reference date, the number of individual non-residential real estate properties, and the method for inspecting individual non-residential real estate prices;
2. The period, procedures, and methods for filing objections.

Article 63 (Base Date for Public Announcement of Non-residential Aggregate Real Estate Prices)
The base date for public announcement of non-residential aggregate real estate prices under the former part of Article 22 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "non-residential aggregate real estate prices") shall be January 1. Provided, That where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems it unavoidable in consideration of the personnel available for surveying and calculating non-residential aggregate real estate prices, the number of non-residential aggregate real estate properties, etc., the Minister may designate certain areas and separately set the base date for public announcement for those areas.

Article 64 (Calculation and Public Announcement of Non-residential Aggregate Real Estate Prices)
(1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to calculate and publicly announce non-residential aggregate real estate prices, the Minister shall calculate and publicly announce such prices by April 30 of each year. Provided, That the prices shall be calculated and publicly announced by September 30 of that year in the case of Article 67 (2) 1 and by April 30 of the following year in the case of subparagraph 2 of that paragraph.
(2) The public announcement of non-residential aggregate real estate prices under Article 22 (1) of the Act shall include the following matters:
1. The location, name, building number, and unit number of the non-residential aggregate real estate;
2. The non-residential aggregate real estate price;
3. The area of the non-residential aggregate real estate;
4. Other matters necessary for the public announcement of non-residential aggregate real estate prices.
(3) When publicly announcing non-residential aggregate real estate prices pursuant to the former part of Article 22 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall publish a notice of the following matters in the Official Gazette, post the non-residential aggregate real estate prices on the Real Estate Publicly Announced Price System, and individually notify the owners of non-residential aggregate real estate:
1. An outline of the matters specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (2);
2. The method for inspecting non-residential aggregate real estate prices;
3. The period, procedures, and methods for filing objections.
(4) Pursuant to the latter part of Article 22 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall provide the matters publicly announced concerning non-residential aggregate real estate prices to the following persons within 10 days from the date of the notice under paragraph (3): <Amended on July 26, 2017>
1. The Minister of the Interior and Safety;
2. The Commissioner of the National Tax Service;
3. The head of a Si/Gun/Gu.

Article 65 (Cases Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Commissioner of the National Tax Service Determines and Publicly Notifies Non-residential Aggregate Real Estate Prices)
Cases where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Commissioner of the National Tax Service separately determines and publicly notifies non-residential aggregate real estate prices pursuant to Article 22 (2) of the Act shall be cases where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Commissioner of the National Tax Service separately determines and publicly notifies non-residential aggregate real estate prices after consulting in advance with the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport on the subject properties, timing, etc. <Amended on July 26, 2017>

Article 66 (Hearing Opinions of Owners, etc. of Non-residential Aggregate Real Estate)
Article 5 (1) and (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the hearing of opinions under Article 22 (3) of the Act.

Article 67 (Non-residential Aggregate Real Estate for Which a Different Base Date for Public Announcement of Non-residential Aggregate Real Estate Prices May Be Set)
(1) Non-residential aggregate real estate for which a different base date for public announcement of non-residential aggregate real estate prices may be set pursuant to Article 22 (5) of the Act shall be real estate falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Non-residential aggregate real estate whose site has been divided or consolidated pursuant to the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data;
2. Non-residential aggregate real estate that has undergone construction, substantial repair, or a change of use under the Building Act;
3. Non-residential aggregate real estate that has become privately owned through sale or otherwise after being owned by the State or a local government and for which there is no non-residential aggregate real estate price.
(2) The term "date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22 (5) of the Act means the date specified in the following subparagraphs:
1. Non-residential aggregate real estate for which a ground specified in any subparagraph of paragraph (1) arose between January 1 and May 31: June 1 of that year;
2. Non-residential aggregate real estate for which a ground specified in any subparagraph of paragraph (1) arose between June 1 and December 31: January 1 of the following year.

Article 68 (Standards for Surveying and Calculating Non-residential Aggregate Real Estate Prices)
(1) When surveying and calculating non-residential aggregate real estate prices pursuant to Article 22 (6) of the Act, if a right of lease on a deposit basis or any other right restricting the use of or the making of profits from the relevant non-residential aggregate real estate has been established, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall calculate the fair price on the assumption that such right does not exist.
(2) Detailed standards for surveying and calculating non-residential aggregate real estate prices under Article 22 of the Act shall be prescribed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport following deliberation by the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values.

Article 69 (Procedures for Surveying and Calculating Non-residential Aggregate Real Estate Prices)
(1) The term "persons with expertise in surveying and calculating real estate prices, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22 (7) of the Act means appraisal corporations, etc. <Amended on October 8, 2020>
(2) A person requested to survey and calculate non-residential aggregate real estate prices pursuant to Article 22 (7) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "non-residential aggregate real estate price survey and calculation institution") shall, after surveying and calculating non-residential aggregate real estate prices and other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, prepare a report on the survey and calculation of non-residential aggregate real estate prices as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport and submit it to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
(3) Upon receiving a report pursuant to paragraph (2), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall provide the report to the following persons: <Amended on July 26, 2017>
1. The Minister of the Interior and Safety;
2. The Commissioner of the National Tax Service;
3. A Mayor/Do Governor;
4. The head of a Si/Gun/Gu.
(4) A person who has been provided with a report pursuant to paragraph (3) may request the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to review the appropriateness of the report.
(5) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may review whether a report submitted pursuant to paragraph (2) is appropriate by using reported actual transaction prices, the appraisal information system, etc.
(6) Where deemed necessary for the review of appropriateness under paragraph (5), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may separately designate a person with expertise in surveying and calculating real estate prices other than the relevant non-residential aggregate real estate price survey and calculation institution and hear that person's opinion.
(7) Where, as a result of the review under paragraph (5), the report is determined to be inappropriate or the survey and calculation of non-residential aggregate real estate prices is deemed to have been performed in violation of relevant statutes and regulations, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may require the relevant non-residential aggregate real estate price survey and calculation institution to correct and resubmit the report.

Article 70 (Grounds for Correcting Non-residential Aggregate Real Estate Prices)
(1) The term "obvious errors prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22 (8) of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where the public announcement procedures under Article 22 of the Act have not been fully implemented;
2. Where major factors affecting non-residential aggregate real estate prices, such as the indication of building and unit numbers and floors, have been incorrectly surveyed.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to correct errors in non-residential aggregate real estate prices pursuant to Article 22 (8) of the Act, the Minister shall determine and publicly announce the corrections following deliberation by the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values. Provided, That deliberation by the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values may be omitted in cases of miscalculations or clerical errors.

CHAPTER 5 COMMITTEES ON PUBLIC ANNOUNCEMENT OF REAL ESTATE VALUES

Article 71 (Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values)
(1) Gender shall be taken into account when forming the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values pursuant to Article 24 (2) of the Act.
(2) The term "central administrative agencies prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 24 (4) of the Act means the following central administrative agencies: <Amended on July 26, 2017; June 2, 2020; December 30, 2025>
1. The Ministry of Finance and Economy;
2. The Ministry of the Interior and Safety;
3. The Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs;
3-2. The Ministry of Health and Welfare;
4. The Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
(3) The chairperson of the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values (hereinafter referred to as the "chairperson") shall represent the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values and exercise overall control over its affairs.
(4) The chairperson shall convene and preside over meetings of the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values.
(5) The Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values shall have one vice chairperson, who shall be nominated by the chairperson from among its members.
(6) The vice chairperson shall assist the chairperson and act on behalf of the chairperson when the chairperson is unable to perform the duties of the office due to unavoidable circumstances.
(7) When both the chairperson and vice chairperson are unable to perform the duties of their offices due to unavoidable circumstances, a member nominated in advance by the chairperson shall act on their behalf.
(8) When convening a meeting of the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values, the chairperson shall individually notify the members no later than three days before the meeting, attaching the agenda items.
(9) A meeting of the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values shall open with a majority of its incumbent members present, and resolutions shall be adopted with the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.
(10) Members of the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values who are not public officials may be paid allowances and travel expenses within budgetary limits.
(11) Detailed matters necessary for the operation of the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (10), shall be prescribed by the chairperson following a resolution of the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values.

Article 72 (Exclusion, Challenge, and Recusal of Members)
(1) A member of the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values shall be excluded from its deliberations and resolutions if the member falls under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Where the member or the member's current or former spouse is a party to the relevant agenda item (including its executives if the party is a corporation, organization, etc.; hereinafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph and subparagraph 2) or is a joint holder of rights or a joint obligor with a party to that agenda item;
2. Where the member is or was a relative of a party to the relevant agenda item;
3. Where the member has given testimony or a statement, provided advice, conducted an investigation or research, provided services, or performed an appraisal concerning the relevant agenda item;
4. Where the member or the corporation, organization, etc. to which the member belongs is or was an agent of a party to the relevant agenda item;
5. Where the member belongs to the same appraisal corporation or appraisal office as a party to the relevant agenda item.
(2) Where there are circumstances that make it difficult to expect impartial deliberation and resolution from a member, a party may apply to the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values to challenge the member, and the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values shall decide on the application by resolution. In such cases, the member who is the subject of the challenge shall not participate in that resolution.
(3) Where a member falls under any ground for exclusion specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1), the member shall voluntarily recuse themself from deliberation and resolution on the relevant agenda item.

Article 73 (Dismissal of Members, etc.)
(1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may dismiss an appointed member of the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values if the member falls under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform their duties due to a mental or physical disability;
2. Where the member has committed misconduct in connection with their duties;
3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable to serve as an appointed member due to neglect of duties, conduct impairing dignity, or other grounds;
4. Where the member expresses that it is difficult for them to perform their duties;
5. Where the member fails to recuse themself despite falling under any subparagraph of Article 72 (1).
(2) A person who has nominated a member pursuant to Article 24 (4) of the Act may withdraw the nomination if the member falls under any subparagraph of paragraph (1).

Article 74 (Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values)
(1) A Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values shall consist of at least 10 and not more than 15 members, including one chairperson, and gender shall be taken into account.
(2) The deputy head of the Si/Gun/Gu shall serve as the chairperson of the Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values. In such cases, if there are two or more deputy heads of the Si/Gun/Gu, the deputy head nominated by the head of the Si/Gun/Gu shall serve as chairperson.
(3) The members of a Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values shall consist of not more than six public officials nominated by the head of the Si/Gun/Gu and persons appointed by the head of the Si/Gun/Gu from among persons falling under any of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on December 18, 2018>
1. A person with extensive knowledge and experience in the public announcement of real estate values or appraisal who is well acquainted with local circumstances;
2. A person recommended by a civic organization (meaning a nonprofit nongovernmental organization under Article 2 of the Assistance for Non-Profit, Non-Governmental Organizations Act).
(4) Articles 72 and 73 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the exclusion, challenge, recusal, and dismissal of members of a Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values.
(5) Matters necessary for the composition and operation of a Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (4), shall be prescribed by ordinance of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu.

CHAPTER 6 SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 74-2 (Formulation of Plans for Reflecting Fair Prices)
(1) When formulating a plan under Article 26-2 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall include the following matters:
1. Target rates of reflection of market prices by type of real estate;
2. The period necessary to achieve the target rates of reflection of market prices by type of real estate and annual plans for achieving those targets;
3. Measures to ensure balance among publicly announced real estate prices;
4. Measures to reflect changes in real estate prices and equity and distinctive characteristics by type, region, and price range.
(2) Where necessary for formulating a plan under Article 26-2 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may request State agencies, local governments, the Board, and other institutions, corporations, or organizations to submit or allow inspection of necessary data or to submit opinions. <Amended on December 8, 2020>

Article 75 (Establishment and Management of the Publicly Announced Price Information System)
(1) The publicly announced price information system under Article 27 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "publicly announced price information system") shall include the following information:
1. Information on prices publicly announced pursuant to the Act;
2. Information on the characteristics of real estate subject to public announcement under subparagraph 1;
3. Other information relating to publicly announced real estate prices.
(2) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport (including a person entrusted with the establishment and management of the publicly announced price information system pursuant to Article 28 (1) 5 of the Act) may provide the information specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) to the following persons. Provided, That the types and content of the information provided may be restricted where there are legitimate grounds, such as the protection of personal information. <Amended on July 26, 2017>
1. The Minister of the Interior and Safety;
2. The Commissioner of the National Tax Service;
3. A Mayor/Do Governor;
4. The head of a Si/Gun/Gu.

Article 75-2 (Disclosure of Minutes)
(1) The term "period prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 27-2 of the Act means three months.
(2) Pursuant to Article 27-2 of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall post on the Real Estate Publicly Announced Price System the minutes of deliberations by the Central Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values that fall under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Deliberations for the public announcement of officially announced standard land prices under Article 3 (1) of the Act;
2. Deliberations for the public announcement of standard housing prices under Article 16 (1) of the Act;
3. Deliberations for the public announcement of multi-family housing prices under the main clause of Article 18 (1) of the Act;
4. Deliberations for the public announcement of standard non-residential real estate prices under Article 20 (1) of the Act;
5. Deliberations for the public announcement of non-residential aggregate real estate prices under the former part of Article 22 (1) of the Act.
(3) Pursuant to Article 27-2 of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall post the minutes of deliberations by the Si/Gun/Gu Committee on Public Announcement of Real Estate Values that fall under any of the following subparagraphs on the bulletin board or website of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu, or request the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to post them on the Real Estate Publicly Announced Price System:
1. Deliberations for the determination and public announcement of officially announced individual land prices under Article 10 (1) of the Act;
2. Deliberations for the determination and public announcement of individual housing prices under Article 17 (1) of the Act;
3. Deliberations for the determination and public announcement of individual non-residential real estate prices under the main clause of Article 21 (1) of the Act.
(4) The term "personally identifying information prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as names and resident registration numbers" in the proviso to Article 27-2 of the Act means information that can identify a specific person, such as a name, resident registration number, address, or position.

Article 76 (Entrustment of Duties)
(1) The term "duties prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 28 (1) 6 of the Act means education and research relating to the duties under subparagraphs 1 through 5 of that paragraph.
(2) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall entrust the duties specified in the subparagraphs of Article 28 (1) of the Act to the Board. <Amended on December 8, 2020>

Article 77 (Processing of Unique Identifying Information)
The head of a relevant administrative agency who has been requested by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to allow inspection of or submit data pursuant to Article 4 of the Act may process data containing resident registration numbers or alien registration numbers under subparagraph 1 or 4 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act where unavoidable for submitting the names and addresses of standard land owners under subparagraph 10 of Article 9.

